    <briefdescription>
<para>Concrete moisture model for a terrain cell. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><ref refid="class_cell_moisture" kindref="compound">CellMoisture</ref> represents a cell influenced by a single <ref refid="class_moisture_source" kindref="compound">MoistureSource</ref>. It manages:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>the current moisture source,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the temperature and relative humidity derived from that source,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>whether the cell is predator-free or competitor-free space,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the cell&apos;s moisture level,</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>the maximum resource capacity density.</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>This class is used by the simulation to compute environmental effects impacting resource availability and animal behavior.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="class_cell_moisture_interface" kindref="compound">CellMoistureInterface</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="class_moisture_source" kindref="compound">MoistureSource</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
